\ The QEMU versatilepb board has a PL181 MMC interface with an SD card.
\ The cards are memory mapped using the ARM advanced peripheral bus (APB).

\ The stack looks like this:
\ - Filesystem
\ - Block device
\ - MMC subsystem
\ - PL181 + SD card driver

\ TODO: Add vocabularies to the target Forth? Custom build for the ARM machine,
\ maybe.

\ ARM systems do not (generally) have a BIOS, and because they use
\ memory-mapped I/O rather than port-based I/O, it's less obvious how to
\ standardize on the locations and types of devices. On a PC architecture,
\ the PCI bus can always be poked at particular standard I/O port numbers and
\ probed to find out what's up. For ARM, the kernel must Just Know where to find
\ each device and what it already is.
\ This is achieved with device trees, and is why there are device-specific
\ builds for ARM systems compared to the general `x86_64` builds of PC Linux.
\ I can hard-code these for now based on the various devices, but certainly if
\ I want some flexibility this will need to become a basic data input.

\ The QEMU versatilepb board has the following (`info mtree` for all):
\ - $1000_0000 x     $1000   ARM sysctl
\ - $1000_5000 x     $1000   PL181 MMC interface to SD Card
\ - $1000_6000 x     $1000   PL050 KMI with PS/2 keyboard (or mouse?)
\ - $1000_7000 x     $1000   PL050 KMI with PS/2 mouse (or keyboard?)
\ - $1000_b000 x     $1000   PL181 MMC interface to SD Card
\ - $1001_0000 x       $10   SMC 91c11 ethernet adapter
\ - $1012_0000 x     $1000   PL110 LCD controller
\ - $3400_0000 x $400_0000   Flash ROM with `-kernel` payload(?)
\ - And then some PCI stuff (hard drive, CD and floppy controllers via SCSI)

\ Programmer's Interface =====================================================
\ Addr Type Width  Reset  Name             Use
\ $000 R W      8      0  MCIPower         Power control register
\ $004 R W     12      0  MCIClock         Clock control register
\ $008 R W     32      0  MCIArgument      Argument register
\ $00c R W     11      0  MMCCommand       Command register
\ $010 R        6      0  MCIRespCmd       Response command register
\ $014 R       32      0  MCIResponse0     Response register 0
\ $018 R       32      0  MCIResponse1     Response register 1
\ $01c R       32      0  MCIResponse2     Response register 2
\ $020 R       31      0  MCIResponse3     Response register 3
\ $024 R W     32      0  MCIDataTimer     Data timer
\ $028 R W     16      0  MCIDataLength    Data length register
\ $02c R W      8      0  MCIDataCtrl      Data control register
\ $030 R       16      0  MCIDataCnt       Data counter
\ $034 R       22      0  MCIStatus        Status register
\ $038   W     11      0  MCIClear         Clear register
\ $03c R W     22      0  MCIMask0         Interrupt 0 mask register
\ $040 R W     22      0  MCIMask1         Interrupt 1 mask register
\ $044 R W      4      0  MCISelect        SD card select register
\ $048 R       15      0  MCIFifoCnt       FIFO counter
\ (reserved)
\ $080 R W     32      0  MCIFIFO          Data FIFO register
\ ... FIFO is 16 words = 64 bytes long ($40)
\ $0bc R W     32      0  MCIFIFO          Data FIFO register
\ $fe0 R        8    $80  MCIPeriphID0     Peripheral ID register  7:0
\ $fe4 R        8    $11  MCIPeriphID1     Peripheral ID register 15:8
\ $fe8 R        8    $04  MCIPeriphID2     Peripheral ID register 23:16
\ $fec R        8    $00  MCIPeriphID3     Peripheral ID register 31:24
\ $ff0 R        8    $0d  MCICellID0       PrimeCell  ID register  7:0
\ $ff4 R        8    $f0  MCICellID1       PrimeCell  ID register 15:8
\ $ff8 R        8    $05  MCICellID2       PrimeCell  ID register 23:16
\ $ffc R        8    $b1  MCICellID3       PrimeCell  ID register 31:24

target definitions

$10005000 CONSTANT pl181
BEGIN-STRUCTURE [pl181]   \  Wdth Rst Name            Use
  FIELD: mci>power        \ RW  8   0 MCIPower        Power control reg
  FIELD: mci>clock        \ RW 12   0 MCIClock        Clock control reg
  FIELD: mci>argument     \ RW 32   0 MCIArgument     Argument reg
  FIELD: mci>command      \ RW 11   0 MMCCommand      Command reg
  FIELD: mci>resp-cmd     \ R   6   0 MCIRespCmd      Response command reg
  FIELD: mci>response0    \ R  32   0 MCIResponse0    Response reg 0
  FIELD: mci>response1    \ R  32   0 MCIResponse1    Response reg 1
  FIELD: mci>response2    \ R  32   0 MCIResponse2    Response reg 2
  FIELD: mci>response3    \ R  32   0 MCIResponse3    Response reg 3
  FIELD: mci>data-timer   \ RW 32   0 MCIDataTimer    Data timer
  FIELD: mci>data-length  \ RW 16   0 MCIDataLength   Data length reg
  FIELD: mci>data-ctrl    \ RW  8   0 MCIDataCtrl     Data control reg
  FIELD: mci>data-counter \ R  16   0 MCIDataCnt      Data counter
  FIELD: mci>status       \ R  22   0 MCIStatus       Status register
  FIELD: mci>clear        \  W 11   0 MCIClear        Clear register
  FIELD: mci>mask0        \ RW 22   0 MCIMask0        Interrupt 0 mask reg
  FIELD: mci>mask1        \ RW 22   0 MCIMask1        Interrupt 1 mask reg
  FIELD: mci>select       \ RW  4   0 MCISelect       SD card select reg
  FIELD: mci>fifo-cnt     \ R  15   0 MCIFifoCnt      FIFO counter
  drop $080
  FIELD: mci>fifo0        \ RW 32   0 MCIFIFO         16 words of FIFO
  drop $fe0
  FIELD: mci>periph-id0   \ R   8 $80 MCIPeriphID0    Peripheral ID reg  7:0
  FIELD: mci>periph-id1   \ R   8 $11 MCIPeriphID1    Peripheral ID reg 15:8
  FIELD: mci>periph-id2   \ R   8 $04 MCIPeriphID2    Peripheral ID reg 23:16
  FIELD: mci>periph-id3   \ R   8 $00 MCIPeriphID3    Peripheral ID reg 31:24
  FIELD: mci>cell-id0     \ R   8 $0d MCICellID0      PrimeCell  ID reg  7:0
  FIELD: mci>cell-id1     \ R   8 $f0 MCICellID1      PrimeCell  ID reg 15:8
  FIELD: mci>cell-id2     \ R   8 $05 MCICellID2      PrimeCell  ID reg 23:16
  FIELD: mci>cell-id3     \ R   8 $b1 MCICellID3      PrimeCell  ID reg 31:24
END-STRUCTURE

: mci-init-controller ( base-addr -- )
  dup   mci>power   dup @   3 or   swap !
  $11f  swap mci>clock !
  \ Wait at least 2ms for the interface and card to be ready.
  2 ms ;

\ MCICommand ($00c, R/W, 11 bits)
\ EPI LRcc cccc
\ E=Enable CPSM; P=Wait for CmdPend before sending command
\ I=Stop timer and wait for interrupt; L=Long response expected
\ R=Wait for a response; c=command index


\ TODO: Rename these, they're not very Forth-y.
 0 CONSTANT SD_CMD_GO_IDLE_STATE
 2 CONSTANT SD_CMD_ALL_SEND_CID
 3 CONSTANT SD_CMD_SEND_RELATIVE_ADDR
 8 CONSTANT SD_CMD_SEND_IF_COND
 9 CONSTANT SD_CMD_SEND_CSD
 7 CONSTANT SD_CMD_SELECT_CARD
55 CONSTANT SD_CMD_APP_CMD
41 CONSTANT SD_CMD_SD_SEND_OP_COND

 $3f CONSTANT MMC_CMD_MASK
$400 CONSTANT MMC_CPSM_ENABLE

1 30 lshift CONSTANT OCR_HCS
1 31 lshift CONSTANT OCR_READY
$ff8000     CONSTANT SD_VOLTAGE_WINDOW
512         CONSTANT BYTES_PER_BLOCK
$40000000   CONSTANT CSD_V2_MASK \ CSD structure version 2.0
256 1024 *  CONSTANT SD_STD_CAPACITY_MULT
512 1024 *  CONSTANT SD_HIGH_CAPACITY_MULT
$ff         CONSTANT SD_BYTE_MASK
$120        CONSTANT CMD55_VALID_RESP

$01 CONSTANT MMC_RSP_PRESENT
$02 CONSTANT MMC_RSP_136
$04 CONSTANT MMC_RSP_CRC
$08 CONSTANT MMC_RSP_BUSY
$10 CONSTANT MMC_RSP_OPCODE
$1f CONSTANT MMC_RSP_MASK

\ Response maps - these are combos of the above flags.
0                                                       CONSTANT MMC_RSP_NONE
MMC_RSP_PRESENT                                         CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R3
MMC_RSP_PRESENT                                         CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R4
MMC_RSP_PRESENT MMC_RSP_CRC or MMC_RSP_OPCODE or    dup CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R1
dup                                                     CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R5
dup                                                     CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R6
dup                                                     CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R7
MMC_RSP_BUSY or                                         CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R1B
MMC_RSP_PRESENT MMC_RSP_136 or MMC_RSP_CRC or           CONSTANT MMC_RSP_R2

1 8 lshift                      CONSTANT MMC_DATA_WRITE
1 9 lshift                      CONSTANT MMC_DATA_READ
MMC_DATA_WRITE MMC_DATA_READ or CONSTANT MMC_DATA_XFER



\ SD card checks:
\ - SD_CMD_SEND_IF_COND, $1aa, MMC_RSP_R7
\ - Retry up to 5 times:
\   - Wait 10ms.
\   - Bail if we're out of retries.
\   - SD_CMD_APP_CMD, 0, MMC_RSP_R1
\     - Retry if the response wasn't CMD55_VALID_RESP
\   - SD_CMD_SD_SEND_OP_COND, OCR_HCS | SD_VOLTAGE_WINDOW, MMC_RSP_R3
\   - Repeat until the resp[0]&OCR_READY bit is nonzero.
\ - If we leave that loop then this is indeed an SD card.
\ - SD_CMD_ALL_SEND_CID, 0, MMC_RSP_R2
\   - Returns card, manufacturer etc. info, dump it for intel!
\ - SD_CMD_SEND_RELATIVE_ADDR, 0, MMC_RSP_R6
\   - Returns the card's RCA, the relative address. (resp[0]>>16)
\ - SD_CMD_SEND_CSD, rca<<16, MMC_RSP_R2
\   - Has the device size etc., see that command.

CREATE mmc-resp 4 cells allot

\ EPI LRcc cccc
\ E=Enable CPSM; P=Wait for CmdPend before sending command
\ I=Stop timer and wait for interrupt; L=Long response expected
\ R=Wait for a response; c=command index
: <pl181-req-flags> ( responds? long? -- cmd-bits )
  MMC_CPSM_ENABLE
  swap MMC_RSP_136 and IF $80 or THEN ( responds? cmd-bits )
  swap                 IF $40 or THEN ;

: <pl181-send> ( cmd arg responds? long? base-addr -- )
  >R <pl181-req-flags> ( cmd arg cmd-bits )
  rot MMC_CMD_MASK and or ( arg cmd )
  ." PL181 addr: " R@   hex. cr
  ." PL181 cmd:  " dup  hex. cr
  ." PL181 arg:  " over hex. cr
  swap R@ mci>argument !  ( cmd )
       R> mci>command ! ;

: <pl181-receive> ( 'resp base-addr -- )
  2dup mci>response0 @   swap !
  2dup mci>response1 @   swap cell+     !
  2dup mci>response2 @   swap 2 cells + !
       mci>response3 @   swap 3 cells + ! ;

: pl181:mmc-request ( cmd arg flags 'resp base-addr -- )
  swap >R >R        ( cmd arg flags    R: 'resp base-addr )
  dup  MMC_RSP_PRESENT and
  swap MMC_RSP_136 and      ( cmd arg responds? long? )
  R@ <pl181-send>           ( R: 'resp base-addr )
  R> R> swap <pl181-receive> ;
  \ TODO: Handle the MMC_DATA_XFER copying and whatnot.

\ CMDn is that plain command.
\ ACMDn is sending a CMD55 first, then CMDn. The "APP_CMD" prefix.
\ Card capacities and standard filesystems:
\ - SDSC supports 8MiB to 2GiB. This is the FAT16 limit due to byte indexes.
\ - SDHC supports 4GiB to 32GiB, which is the limits of the FAT32 filesystem.
\ - SDXC supports 64GiB to 2TiB, using exFAT and 32-bit block indexes.
\ - SDUC exists (128TiB) using exFAT, extending the address to a 38-bit LBA.

\ The initialization sequence (see https://elm-chan.org/docs/mmc/rc/sdinit.png
\ though note that it's for SPI mode and doesn't match perfectly) is this:
\ - CMD0 SD_CMD_GO_IDLE_STATE to put all cards into standby mode.
\   - On an error or no response: unknown/no card.
\ - CMD8 SD_CMD_SEND_IF_COND with arg $1aa
\ - Check low 12 bits of R7 response:
\   - Mismatch: Unknown card
\   - Matches 0x1aa: See SDv2+ below.
\   - Error or no response: See SDv1 below.
\
\ SDv2+ (common):
\ - ACMD41, arg $40000000, await R1 response
\   - Error, no response or timeout: Unknown card
\   - Response $01: repeat ACMD41 - loop can take 1000ms!
\   - Response $00: Proceed
\ - CMD58: Check CCS bit of OCR
\   - 0: SDv2 with byte addresses
\   - 1: SDv2 with block addresses
\ - **If byte addressing** use CMD16 $200 to force a 512B block.
\ - Success!

\ SDv1 - Similar, but disregard for now, they're really old.

\ Sending commands ===========================================================
\ Raw command word that takes every arg literally.
DEFER <mmc-send-cmd> ( cmd arg flags 'resp base-addr -- )
' pl181:mmc-request IS <mmc-send-cmd>

CREATE mmc-response 4 cells allot
0 VALUE mmc-base

\ Cooked command word that uses the global response and base.
: mmc-send-cmd ( cmd# arg resp-type -- )
  mmc-response mmc-base <mmc-send-cmd> ;

\ R1 response bits
1  CONSTANT RESP_IDLE
2  CONSTANT RESP_ERASE_RESET
4  CONSTANT RESP_ILLEGAL_CMD
8  CONSTANT RESP_CRC_ERROR
16 CONSTANT RESP_ERASE_SEQ_ERROR
32 CONSTANT RESP_ADDR_ERROR
64 CONSTANT RESP_PARAM_ERROR

\ Clears all 11 "static" status bits.
: mmc-clear-status ( -- )
  $7ff mmc-base mci>clear ! ;

\ Sends CMD58(0) and read R3. Bit 30 is set for SDHC and SDXC.
\ : mmc-sd-sdhc/xc? ( -- sdhc? )
\   mmc-clear-status
\   58 0 MMC_RSP_R1 mmc-send-cmd
\   ." Status: " pl181 mci>status             @ hex. cr
\   ." Resp 0: " pl181 mmc-response           @ hex. cr
\   ." Resp 1: " pl181 mmc-response cell+     @ hex. cr
\   ." Resp 2: " pl181 mmc-response 2 cells + @ hex. cr
\   ." Resp 3: " pl181 mmc-response 3 cells + @ hex. cr
\   false ;

\ 5C0
\ Low 11 bits - static, these latch until cleared.
\ %101 1100 0000
\  ||| |||| |||+- CmdCrcFail   Command response received, CRC fail
\  ||| |||| ||+-- DataCrcFail  Data block sent/received, CRC fail
\  ||| |||| |+--- CmdTimeOut   Command response timeout
\  ||| |||| +---- DataTimeOut  Data timeout
\  ||| ||||
\  ||| |||+------ TxUnderrun   Transmit FIFO underrun error
\  ||| ||+------- RxUnderrun   Receive FIFO overrun error
\  ||| |+-------- CmdRespEnd   Command response received, CRC ok
\  ||| +--------- CmdSent      Command sent, no response required
\  |||
\  ||+----------- DataEnd      Data end (data counter is zero)
\  |+------------ StartBitErr  Start bit not detected in wide mode?
\  +------------  DataBlockEnd Data block sent/received, CRC ok

\ High 11 bits - dynamic, these are live values
\ %00 0000 0000 0
\  || |||| |||| +-- CmdActive       Command transfer in progress
\  || |||| ||||
\  || |||| |||+---- TxActive        Data transmit in progress
\  || |||| ||+----- RxActive        Date receive in progress
\  || |||| |+------ TxFifoHalfEmpty Transmit FIFO half empty
\  || |||| +------- RxFifoHalfFull  Receive FIFO half empty
\  || ||||
\  || |||+--------- TxFifoFull      Transmit FIFO full
\  || ||+---------- RxFifoFull      Receive FIFO full
\  || |+----------- TxFifoEmpty     Transmit FIFO empty
\  || +------------ RxFifoEmpty     Receive FIFO empty
\  ||
\  |+-------------- TxDataAvbl      Data available in transmit FIFO
\  +--------------- RxDataAvbl      Data available in receive FIFO

: .mmc-status ( -- )
  mmc-base mci>status @
  dup $000001 and IF ." S - Command response CRC failed" cr THEN
  dup $000002 and IF ." S - Data block CRC failed" cr THEN
  dup $000004 and IF ." S - Command response timeout" cr THEN
  dup $000008 and IF ." S - Data timeout" cr THEN
  dup $000010 and IF ." S - Transmit FIFO underrun error" cr THEN
  dup $000020 and IF ." S - Receive FIFO overrun error" cr THEN
  dup $000040 and IF ." S - Command response received, CRC ok" cr THEN
  dup $000080 and IF ." S - Command sent, no response required" cr THEN
  dup $000100 and IF ." S - Data end (counter is zero)" cr THEN
  dup $000200 and IF ." S - Start bit not detected in wide mode?" cr THEN
  dup $000400 and IF ." S - Data block done, CRC ok" cr THEN

  dup $000800 and IF ." D - Command transfer in progress" cr THEN
  dup $001000 and IF ." D - Data transmit in progress" cr THEN
  dup $002000 and IF ." D - Data receive in progress" cr THEN
  dup $004000 and IF ." D - Transmit FIFO half empty" cr THEN
  dup $008000 and IF ." D - Receive FIFO half empty" cr THEN
  dup $010000 and IF ." D - Transmit FIFO full" cr THEN
  dup $020000 and IF ." D - Receive FIFO full" cr THEN
  dup $040000 and IF ." D - Transmit FIFO empty" cr THEN
  dup $080000 and IF ." D - Receive FIFO empty" cr THEN
  dup $100000 and IF ." D - Data available in transmit FIFO" cr THEN
      $200000 and IF ." D - Data available in receive FIFO" cr THEN ;

\ Command wrappers ===========================================================
\ CMD0, 0 arg, no response.
: mmc-cmd-go-idle ( -- ) 0 0 0 mmc-send-cmd ;

\ CMD8, $1aa, R7 response
: mmc-cmd-send-if-cond ( -- match? )
  8 $1aa MMC_RSP_R7 mmc-send-cmd
  \ Expects to get $1aa back in the low 12 bits to match an SDv2 card.
  mmc-response @   $3ff and   $1aa = ;

\ ACMD41 (55+41), set bit 30 on for high capacity support + voltage, R1 response
: mmc-cmd-app-send-op-cond ( -- ready? )
  55 0       0          mmc-send-cmd   \ CMD55, 0, no response (ACMD prefix)
  mmc-clear-status
  \ CMD41 with HCS bit + voltage window. Borrowed this value from embox.
  \ TODO: Real hardware will need that set properly.
  41   OCR_HCS $ff8000 or   MMC_RSP_R1 mmc-send-cmd
  mmc-response @
  ." ACMD41 response: " dup hex.
  1 31 lshift and 0<> ." READY bit " dup . ;

: mmc-poll-initialize ( -- done? )
  mmc-cmd-app-send-op-cond ;


\ Repeatedly sends ACMD41 until the card replies it's ready.
\ Times out at 2 seconds.
: mmc-sd-init ( -- ? )
  \ ticks @ >R
  5 BEGIN
    100 ms mmc-poll-initialize 0=
  WHILE \ Not initialized yet
    1- dup 0= IF drop 203 throw THEN
  REPEAT drop true ;

\ Reads the CID register, identifying the SD controller.
\ Long response, so it lives in the response buffer.
: mmc-cid@ ( -- )
  SD_CMD_ALL_SEND_CID 0 MMC_RSP_R2 mmc-send-cmd ; \ CMD2, 0, R2

: .spacer ( -- )
  ." ==========================================" cr ;

: month>short-name ( month-0-based -- c-addr u )
  3 *
  S" JanFebMarAprMayJunJulAugSepOctNovDec" ( month-offset c-addr u-all )
  drop +   3 ;

: th-resp@ ( 0..3 -- x )
  cells mmc-base mci>response0 + @ ;

\ Prints the CID details from the MCI response cells.
: .mmc-cid ( -- )
  .spacer
  ." MMC CID: raw " 4 0 DO i th-resp@ hex. LOOP cr
  ." Manufacturer ID: " 0 th-resp@ 24 rshift hex. cr
  ." OEM/OID:         " 0 th-resp@ 8  rshift $ffff and hex. cr
  ." Product name:    "
    0 th-resp@ $ff and emit
    1 th-resp@
      dup 24 rshift $ff and emit
      dup 16 rshift $ff and emit
      dup  8 rshift $ff and emit
                    $ff and emit cr
  ." Revision:        " 2 th-resp@ 24 rshift $ff and hex. cr
  ." Serial number:   "
    2 th-resp@ $ffffff and 8 lshift
    3 th-resp@ 24 rshift $ff and   or hex. cr

  ." Date:            "
  \ ssssssss  DDDDDDDD yyyymmmm ________
  3 th-resp@          \ D=decade, y=year of decade, m=month (0=Jan)
  8 rshift $ffff and
  dup $f and >R                 ( DDym   R: month-0-based )
  dup 8 rshift 10 *             ( DDym decade-years   R: month-0-based )
  swap 4 rshift $f and + 2000 + ( year   R: month-0-based )
  R> month>short-name type space . cr ;


\ CMD3, 0, R6 - gets the RCA for the card.
: mmc-send-relative-addr ( -- rca )
  3 0 MMC_RSP_R6 mmc-send-cmd
  0 th-resp@ 16 rshift $ffff and ;

\ In SDHC and SDXC cards, there's a size field in the low byte of resp[1] and
\ upper 2 bytes of resp[2] that is the number of 512KiB units minus 1.
\ 24 bits shifted up by 19 makes a 43-bit number, so it's double cell.
: mmc-size-high ( -- ud-bytes )
  1 th-resp@ $ff and 16 lshift
  2 th-resp@ 16 rshift $ffff and or   1+    ( 512KiB-units )
  \ Shifting up by 19, but that overflows. Low cell is that shift, high cell is
  \ shifted right by 13.
  dup 19 lshift   swap 13 rshift ;

\ In SDSC, it's the low 10 bits of resp[1], +1, times 4, times 256KiB blocks.
\ That's a shift of 12 bits by 20 = 32 bits, so the high cell is always 0.
: mmc-size-std ( -- ud-bytes )
  1 th-resp@ $3ff and   1+   20 lshift   0 ;

: mmc-csd@ ( rca -- ud-bytes hc/xc? )
  \ CMD9, rca<<16, R2 - get the CSD describing the inserted card.
  16 lshift   9 swap   MMC_RSP_R2 mmc-send-cmd
  0 th-resp@ OCR_HCS and IF \ High capacity
    mmc-size-high true ELSE mmc-size-std false THEN ;

\ TODO: Hard-coding this to a single card.
: mmc-select-card ( rca -- )
  16 lshift   SD_CMD_SELECT_CARD swap   MMC_RSP_R1B mmc-send-cmd ;


CREATE test-buf 512 chars allot

\ MCIDataCtrl: bbbb DsRE - block size 2^b, (D)MA, (s)tream, (R)ead, (E)nable
\ For a read we want: 512B (b = 2^9), read (1) and enable (1)
\ TODO: Embox uses 8 = 256 rather than rather than 9 = 512? Trying that.
$83         CONSTANT mci-read-settings

1 21 lshift CONSTANT mci-status-data-avbl

: mmc-read-block ( buffer blk# -- )
  \ CMD17 to read a block, arg is offset - blocks or bytes? R1 + data.
  17 swap   MMC_RSP_R1B MMC_DATA_READ or   mmc-send-cmd
  512 mmc-base mci>data-length !             \ Data length is 512 bytes
  mci-read-settings mmc-base mci>data-ctrl ! \ And set the read config
  \ Now loop to read the words out.
  512 BEGIN ( buffer remaining )
    \ Busy-wait for the receive flag.
    \ ." Waiting for data to be available..." cr
    BEGIN mmc-base mci>status @   mci-status-data-avbl and UNTIL
    \ ." Data ready! Reading a word to " over hex. ." remaining " dup . cr
    \ Read a word ( buffer remaining )
    >R   mmc-base mci>fifo0 @
    \ ." Got word: " dup hex. cr
    over !   cell+
    R> ( buffer' remaining )
    cell -
  dup 0= UNTIL 2drop ;

\ XXX: START HERE: Got it! I successfully read a block from the disk!
\ Some tidying of the code is probably in order and then I'll consider how
\ to rig up block devices more concretely.

: mmc-go ( -- )
  pl181 TO mmc-base
  pl181 mci-init-controller
  \ Setup process for PL181 SD cards:
  \ - [x] GO IDLE
  \ - [x] SEND_IF_COND, $1aa, R7, check response is also $1aa.
  \ - 5x retry:
  \   - [x] Wait 10ms
  \   - [x] Send ACMD41 with the voltage and HC/XC support bit, R3
  \   - [x] Expect the OCR_READY bit in reply
  \ - [x] Check the voltage window in the ACMD41 response - TODO: real hardware
  \ - [x] Send CMD2, 0, R2 and read the CID manufacturer etc.
  \ - [x] Print that for debugging.
  \ - [x] Send SEND_RELATIVE_ADDR, 0, R6 to get the RCA of the card.
  \ - [x] Send CSD to get card details, SEND_CSD, rca<<16, R2
  \ - [x] Dump that for debugging.
  \ - [x] V2 cards return bit 30 set in resp[0], use block addressing.
  \   - V1 cards don't, use byte addressing.
  \ - [x] Either way, compute the card size and print it.
  \ - [ ] Configure the OS's block device with the total size, block size, etc.
  \ - [x] Send SELECT_CARD, rca<<16, R1B to get ready to use the card.

  mmc-cmd-go-idle
  mmc-cmd-send-if-cond   0= IF 202 throw THEN
  mmc-sd-init ." SD init: " . cr
  100 ms
  mmc-cid@ .mmc-cid

  mmc-send-relative-addr ( rca )
  ." SD card RCA: " dup hex. cr
  dup mmc-csd@   ( rca ud-bytes hc/xc? )
  ." SDHC/SDXC? " . cr
  ." SD card size: "
    2dup hex <# #s #> type
    4 spaces decimal <# #s #> type cr  ( rca )
  mmc-select-card

  test-buf 0 mmc-read-block
  10 ms
  .mmc-status   mmc-clear-status

  .spacer
  test-buf 512 type
  cr .spacer cr
;
